 farming systems","note":"Compost, farm-made inputs, cover crops & green manures, regenerative agriculture, moving from chemical to organic, certification. · 6 maps · 490 ideas · 126 KB","manas":{"map":"soil-p-systems","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-research","topic":"🔬 Research & innovation","note":"The latest science and technology worldwide, and the milestones that brought us here. · 3 maps · 247 ideas · 74 KB","manas":{"map":"soil-p-research","part":"research","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-index","topic":"🔤 Strains & names A–Z","note":"Every organism and topic: tap one to open the map that explains it.","children":[{"id":"soil-root-ix0","topic":"6-PP (6-pentyl-α-pyrone)","note":"Coconut-smelling volatile from Trichoderma atroviride that slows pathogens and stimulates roots.","manas":{"map":"soil-trichoderma","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix1","topic":"Aflatoxin (Aspergillus flavus)","note":"Poison from moulds on grain and nuts.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-storage","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix2","topic":"Anabaena & Nostoc (BGA)","note":"Blue-green algae that fix nitrogen in flooded rice.","manas":{"map":"soil-azospirillum","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix3","topic":"Aphids","note":"Sap-sucking insects that spread viruses.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-sucking","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix4","topic":"Aspergillus & Penicillium (PSF)","note":"Phosphate solubilizing fungi.","manas":{"map":"soil-psb","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix5","topic":"Azolla","note":"Water fern that carries nitrogen-fixing Anabaena; green manure for rice.","manas":{"map":"soil-azospirillum","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix6","topic":"Azospirillum","note":"Associative nitrogen fixer on roots of cereals, millets and grasses.","manas":{"map":"soil-azospirillum","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix7","topic":"Azotobacter (azoto, free-living N fixer)","note":"Aerobic soil bacterium that fixes nitrogen on its own; adds tens of kg N/ha, not hundreds. See also Rhizobium, Azospirillum.","manas":{"map":"soil-azotobacter","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix8","topic":"Azotobacter chroococcum","note":"Free-living aerobic nitrogen fixer for non-legume crops.","manas":{"map":"soil-azotobacter","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix9","topic":"Bacillus megaterium (PSB)","note":"Phosphate solubilizing bacterium.","manas":{"map":"soil-psb","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix10","topic":"Bacillus mucilaginosus (KSB)","note":"Potassium solubilizing bacterium.","manas":{"map":"soil-kmb","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix11","topic":"Bacillus subtilis / amyloliquefaciens","note":"Spore-forming biocontrol and growth-promoting bacteria.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix12","topic":"Bacillus thuringiensis (Bt)","note":"Bacterium whose crystal proteins kill caterpillars and some larvae.","manas":{"map":"soil-biopesticides","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix13","topic":"Bacillus velezensis","note":"Spore-forming biocontrol bacterium; many former B. amyloliquefaciens.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix14","topic":"Bacterial wilt (Ralstonia)","note":"Bacterial wilt of potato, tomato and pepper.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-wilts","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix15","topic":"Bactrocera dorsalis","note":"Oriental fruit fly, a major mango pest in Africa.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-fruitflies","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix16","topic":"Banana weevil","note":"Beetle whose larvae tunnel banana corms.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-beetles","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix17","topic":"Beauveria bassiana","note":"Fungus that infects insects (white muscardine).","manas":{"map":"soil-biopesticides","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix18","topic":"Berlese and Baermann funnels","note":"How soil animals and nematodes are counted.","manas":{"map":"soil-food-web","part":"soilsci","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix19","topic":"Biochar","note":"Charcoal made for soil; stable carbon, habitat for microbes.","manas":{"map":"soil-regenerative","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix20","topic":"Black rot of brassicas","note":"Xanthomonas bacterial disease of cabbage and kale.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-bacterial","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix21","topic":"Blossom-end rot","note":"Calcium shortage plus water stress on watermelon.","manas":{"map":"soil-crop-cucurbits","part":"vegetables","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix22","topic":"Bradyrhizobium","note":"Slow-growing rhizobia, e.g. for soybean and cowpea groups.","manas":{"map":"soil-rhizobium","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix23","topic":"Cassava mosaic & brown streak","note":"Whitefly-spread cassava viruses.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-viruses","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix24","topic":"Catch crop / living mulch","note":"Fast cereal that holds leftover nitrogen; low legume under the main crop.","manas":{"map":"soil-cover-crops","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix25","topic":"Coffee berry borer","note":"Beetle that bores into coffee berries.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-beetles","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix26","topic":"Coffee berry disease","note":"Colletotrichum kahawae, a major coffee disease in Kenya.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-blights","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix27","topic":"Coffee leaf rust","note":"Hemileia vastatrix rust on coffee leaves.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-mildews-rusts","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix28","topic":"Cotesia","note":"Parasitoid wasps of caterpillars such as stemborers and fall armyworm.","manas":{"map":"soil-natural-enemies","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix29","topic":"Crotalaria (sunn hemp)","note":"Upright 3–4 month green manure, also a vegetable.","manas":{"map":"soil-cover-crops","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix30","topic":"Cucumber (Cucumis sativus)","note":"Tango; staking, drip, harvest immature.","manas":{"map":"soil-crop-cucurbits","part":"vegetables","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix31","topic":"Cysts (Azotobacter)","note":"Thick-walled resting cells that survive drying and heat, then germinate when moisture returns.","manas":{"map":"soil-azotobacter","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix32","topic":"DAPG (2,4-diacetylphloroglucinol)","note":"Antifungal made by some Pseudomonas; behind take-all decline.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix33","topic":"Desmodium (silverleaf, greenleaf)","note":"Perennial legume: the 'push' intercrop and a green-manure cover crop.","manas":{"map":"soil-push-pull","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix34","topic":"Diamondback moth","note":"Caterpillar pest of cabbage and kale.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-caterpillars","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix35","topic":"Disease-suppressive soil","note":"Soils whose own microbes keep a pathogen in check.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix36","topic":"Earthworms","note":"Raise yields about 25% on average when residues are returned.","manas":{"map":"soil-food-web","part":"soilsci","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix37","topic":"Eisenia fetida & Eudrilus eugeniae","note":"Composting earthworms for vermicompost.","manas":{"map":"soil-compost","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix38","topic":"Epilachna beetle (melon ladybird)","note":"Spotted beetle that skeletonises cucurbit leaves.","manas":{"map":"soil-crop-cucurbits","part":"vegetables","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix39","topic":"Fall armyworm (Spodoptera frugiperda)","note":"Invasive maize caterpillar in Africa since 2016.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-caterpillars","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix40","topic":"Frateuria aurantia (KMB)","note":"Potash mobilizing bacterium.","manas":{"map":"soil-kmb","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix41","topic":"Fusarium wilt","note":"Soil fungus that blocks water vessels.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-wilts","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix42","topic":"Gliotoxin / gliovirin","note":"Antifungal metabolites of Trichoderma virens Q and P strains.","manas":{"map":"soil-trichoderma","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix43","topic":"Glomalin / GRSP","note":"Soil 'glue' linked to mycorrhiza; still debated.","manas":{"map":"soil-food-web","part":"soilsci","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix44","topic":"Gluconacetobacter diazotrophicus","note":"Nitrogen-fixing bacterium living inside sugarcane.","manas":{"map":"soil-azospirillum","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix45","topic":"Green manure / cover crop","note":"Legumes grown to feed and protect the soil.","manas":{"map":"soil-cover-crops","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix46","topic":"Humic & fulvic acids","note":"Biostimulants from decomposed organic matter.","manas":{"map":"soil-biostimulants","part":"nutrition","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix47","topic":"Induced systemic resistance (ISR)","note":"Root microbes prime the whole plant's defences.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix48","topic":"Lablab (dolichos, njahi) cv Rongai","note":"Food, fodder and cover crop for dry-land conservation agriculture.","manas":{"map":"soil-cover-crops","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix49","topic":"Lactic acid bacteria, yeast, photosynthetic bacteria","note":"The groups in Effective Microorganisms (EM).","manas":{"map":"soil-compost","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix50","topic":"Ladybird beetles","note":"Predators of aphids, scales and mites.","manas":{"map":"soil-natural-enemies","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix51","topic":"Larger grain borer","note":"Storage beetle of maize and cassava in East Africa.","manas":{"map":"soil-pest-storage","part":"pests","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix52","topic":"Late blight (Phytophthora infestans)","note":"Fast-spreading disease of potato and tomato.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-blights","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix53","topic":"Lecanicillium lecanii","note":"Fungus against sucking pests like whitefly, aphids, mealybug.","manas":{"map":"soil-biopesticides","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix54","topic":"Maize lethal necrosis (MLN)","note":"Virus disease of maize in East Africa.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-viruses","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix55","topic":"Melon fruit fly (Bactrocera cucurbitae)","note":"Bag fruit, traps, evening pyrethrum.","manas":{"map":"soil-crop-cucurbits","part":"vegetables","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix56","topic":"Metarhizium anisopliae","note":"Fungus that infects insects (green muscardine), e.g. termites, beetles.","manas":{"map":"soil-biopesticides","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix57","topic":"Microbial necromass","note":"Dead microbes: a main source of stable soil carbon.","manas":{"map":"soil-food-web","part":"soilsci","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix58","topic":"Mucuna (velvet bean)","note":"Fast cover that suppresses weeds and striga; seeds toxic (L-dopa).","manas":{"map":"soil-cover-crops","part":"systems","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix59","topic":"Mycorrhizal network (wood wide web)","note":"What the evidence does and does not show.","manas":{"map":"soil-food-web","part":"soilsci","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix60","topic":"Napier grass / Brachiaria Mulato II","note":"Trap ('pull') grasses that attract stemborer moths and feed cattle.","manas":{"map":"soil-push-pull","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix61","topic":"Neem (Azadirachta indica)","note":"Botanical pesticide: azadirachtin antifeedant and growth regulator.","manas":{"map":"soil-botanicals","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix62","topic":"Nitrogenase","note":"The enzyme that breaks the N≡N bond; molybdenum type with vanadium and iron backups in Azotobacter.","manas":{"map":"soil-azotobacter","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix63","topic":"NPV (nucleopolyhedrovirus)","note":"Insect viruses specific to certain caterpillars.","manas":{"map":"soil-biopesticides","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix64","topic":"Powdery & downy mildew of cucurbits","note":"White talc on top vs yellow spots with grey fuzz below.","manas":{"map":"soil-crop-cucurbits","part":"vegetables","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix65","topic":"Powdery mildew","note":"White powdery fungal growth on leaves.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-mildews-rusts","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix66","topic":"Pseudomonas fluorescens","note":"Biocontrol bacterium: siderophores, antibiotics, induced resistance.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix67","topic":"Pseudomonas protegens","note":"Fluorescens-group biocontrol bacterium (Pf-5, CHA0).","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix68","topic":"Pseudomonas striata (PSB)","note":"Phosphate solubilizing bacterium.","manas":{"map":"soil-psb","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix69","topic":"Pumpkin & butternut (Cucurbita)","note":"Malenge/boga; organic production guide.","manas":{"map":"soil-crop-cucurbits","part":"vegetables","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix70","topic":"Purpureocillium lilacinum","note":"Fungus that attacks nematode eggs.","manas":{"map":"soil-biopesticides","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix71","topic":"Push–pull (icipe)","note":"Desmodium between maize rows plus a Napier/Brachiaria border against stemborers, fall armyworm and striga.","manas":{"map":"soil-push-pull","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix72","topic":"Pyrethrum","note":"Botanical insecticide from Chrysanthemum flowers; Kenya a leading producer.","manas":{"map":"soil-botanicals","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix73","topic":"Pythium & damping-off","note":"Water moulds that kill seedlings.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-root-rots","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix74","topic":"Ralstonia (bacterial wilt)","note":"The wilt bacterium, once classed as a Pseudomonas.","manas":{"map":"soil-pseudomonas","part":"protection","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix75","topic":"Rhizobium","note":"Forms nodules on legume roots and fixes nitrogen inside them.","manas":{"map":"soil-rhizobium","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix76","topic":"Rhizophagus / Glomus (AMF)","note":"Arbuscular mycorrhizal fungi that extend roots.","manas":{"map":"soil-mycorrhiza","part":"microbes","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix77","topic":"Rock phosphate","note":"Slow organic-allowed phosphorus source; works best with PSB and in acid soils.","manas":{"map":"soil-organic-fertilizers","part":"nutrition","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix78","topic":"Root-knot nematodes (Meloidogyne)","note":"Microscopic worms that cause root galls.","manas":{"map":"soil-dis-nematodes","part":"diseases","library":"soil"}},{"id":"soil-root-ix79","topic":"Seaweed extracts (Ascophyllum)","note":"Biostimulants that help plants cope with stress.","manas":{"map":"soil-biostimulants","